d to, the following: \u2022volatility in the cost or availability of inputs to our businesses (including raw materials, energy and other supplies and freight); \u2022disruptions or inefficiencies in our supply chain, tariffs, inflation, highly pathogenic avian influenza and other agricultural diseases and pests, labor shortages, public health crises, weather events and fires and other events beyond our control; 32 Table of Contents\n"}
